# Scan Community Patterns

## When to Use
Periodically (monthly) to find new patterns from the AI coding assistant community. Invoke by asking: "scan community for new patterns".

## Key Repositories to Check

**Claude Code**: awesome-claude-code, ChrisWiles/claude-code-showcase, diet103/claude-code-infrastructure-showcase
**OpenCode**: awesome-opencode, zenobi-us/opencode-skillful, malhashemi/opencode-skills
**Cursor**: community rule collections, cursor forum best practices
**General**: neurofoo/agent-skills (marketplace patterns)

## What to Look For
- Hook patterns (auto-activation, validation, secret protection)
- Skill architecture (progressive disclosure, resource management)
- Distribution (install flows, marketplace, updates)
- Memory/context (token management, compression, caching)
- Multi-agent (orchestration, switching, specialized agents)
- Cursor-specific (glob patterns, description optimization, rule composition)

## Evaluation Criteria
- Do we have this already? Better or worse?
- Would it reduce user errors during app building?
- Would it improve token efficiency?
- Effort to implement? (low/medium/high)

## Output
Write findings to `packages/agent-pack/src/core/community-scan-YYYY-MM.md` with: sources checked, patterns found, recommendations, action items.
